WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.920
Dallas marks Tesla's second city for public cybercab rides, giving regulators and riders a fresh look at unsupervised operations in real traffic. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 675. Built in Starlink comes next, then Optimus Scale, and a model y with no wheel, plus first principles. Purpose-built cybercabs are now bookable in mixed urban traffic after the Austin launch, the Defiant Reports. Austin and Dallas are the only cities where the cybercab operates for the

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:36.310
public so far. Elon Musk, in comments carried by digital today, said built-in Starlink should

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:41.470
reach all Tesla models toward the end of next year. The feature will support unsupervised

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:47.290
full-self driving or FSD with high bandwidth links for work and entertainment. He was

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:52.430
answering an ex-user who asked about embedded Starlink beyond the CyberCab. He noted the

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:57.590
connection will matter for passengers who need reliable bandwidth on remote roads. Starlink

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:02.970
remains unavailable in China because it is illegal there. Every cybercab now running in Dallas

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:09.310
already carries the roof integrated antenna. Tesla AI lead Ashok Ellis Swami confirmed that antenna

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:15.470
currently handles only fleet management, navigation and customer service, not passenger streaming.

00:01:16.426 --> 00:01:20.646
Tesla set a 2027 target for scaling optimist production and deployment.

00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:26.786
Tech Republic reports. That timeline covers both internal factory use and external sales.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:33.186
Autowipers on version 15 now adjust more naturally to changing rain, instead of jumping to maximum

00:01:33.186 --> 00:01:36.906
speed and staying there, and owner reported through Tesla Roddy.

00:01:37.466 --> 00:01:40.986
The previous behavior locked at the fastest setting regardless of conditions.

00:01:41.566 --> 00:01:45.086
The change showed up in the first real-world test of the updated software.

00:01:46.216 --> 00:01:51.536
Owners testing FSD version 15 say the car picks the correct parking orientation more reliably

00:01:51.536 --> 00:01:52.716
than version 14.

00:01:52.716 --> 00:01:58.156
driver still cannot choose pull-in versus back-in themselves. One tester said

00:01:58.156 --> 00:02:03.316
version 14 reached roughly 90% accuracy on that choice. No issues with the new

00:02:03.316 --> 00:02:08.385
version have been reported so far. Superchargers, mega-chargers, and destination

00:02:08.385 --> 00:02:13.265
chargers now take a wider set of in-app issue reports. Tesla charging said.

00:02:13.765 --> 00:02:19.025
Those reports root directly to the 24-7 operations team. The extra categories are

00:02:19.025 --> 00:02:23.425
meant to speed fixes by giving that team more precise information about each problem.

00:02:24.085 --> 00:02:26.585
Owners can flag those issues without leaving the vehicle.

00:02:27.566 --> 00:02:32.166
Operating costs on the CyberCab would come in lower than rival robotaxies at the same

00:02:32.166 --> 00:02:32.466
fare.

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.866
Elon Musk said in remarks carried by EVXL.

00:02:36.566 --> 00:02:39.406
The claim centers on vehicle design and fleet economics.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.706
The comparison assumes rivals keep similar pricing.

00:02:43.799 --> 00:02:49.639
A steering wheel free model Y is in development for Robotaxi fleets, with USA Today describing

00:02:49.639 --> 00:02:52.779
a cabin that seats up to 7 and drops manual controls.

00:02:53.479 --> 00:02:58.079
The variant is aimed at fleet operators who want maximum passenger capacity and no

00:02:58.079 --> 00:02:59.099
driver intervention.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:03.159
Production timing stays tied to the wider Robotaxi rollout.

00:03:04.063 --> 00:03:09.643
Stormwatch mode automatically charges power wall units to 100% before forecasted severe

00:03:09.643 --> 00:03:10.043
weather.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:14.503
Tesla Energy said, the aim is to keep homes powered during outages.

00:03:15.023 --> 00:03:18.203
The mode trips off weather alerts and runs without owner input.

00:03:18.203 --> 00:03:23.123
It applies to existing Powerwall installations that receive the latest software update.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:27.256
A Tesla Solar customer with a 16 panel array was told,

00:03:27.796 --> 00:03:32.576
the cooldown reports that the company would not support adding panels even though roof space remains.

00:03:33.316 --> 00:03:36.756
That owner wanted more output and received no official upgrade path.

00:03:37.456 --> 00:03:43.036
Tesla's current process treats each installation as a standalone project rather than an expandable system.

00:03:43.036 --> 00:03:48.492
Manitoba ended electric vehicle or EV purchase rebates as a budget measure.

00:03:49.032 --> 00:03:52.012
The province's top civil servant told the Winnipeg Free Press.

00:03:52.552 --> 00:03:56.132
The decision applies across all EV brands, not only Tesla.

00:03:57.201 --> 00:04:01.681
Used Tesla asking prices climbed to an average of $34,109.

00:04:02.261 --> 00:04:06.781
The cooldown found, as sales volume dropped 5.4%.

00:04:06.781 --> 00:04:10.781
The shift reflects tighter supply of late model vehicles on the used market.

00:04:10.781 --> 00:04:16.881
it. The data covers listings across major platforms in recent weeks. Higher prices have coincided

00:04:16.881 --> 00:04:22.403
with fewer transactions completing. Quick notes from the rest of the day, Tesla posted

00:04:22.403 --> 00:04:28.003
that version 15 protects wheels and tires by avoiding potholes. Hydro Magog, the Quebec

00:04:28.003 --> 00:04:33.943
utility, began a program drive Tesla Canada reports that gives bill credits for charging

00:04:33.943 --> 00:04:39.623
during low-demand hours. Tesla released footage of FSD version 15 driving through desert

00:04:39.623 --> 00:04:44.723
terrain at sunrise. Put the antenna in the body and the car no longer leans on

00:04:44.723 --> 00:04:49.043
cellular networks that change with the town and the carrier. It carries its own

00:04:49.043 --> 00:04:53.483
high bandwidth link from day one. That is a different assumption about what a vehicle

00:04:53.483 --> 00:04:58.023
is allowed to be when the local tower drops out. The panel sits flush in the roof.

00:04:58.543 --> 00:05:02.663
You see it as a square cutout. Engineering teams have roughly 12 months to

00:05:02.663 --> 00:05:07.403
finish the same integration across the Model 3, the Model Y, and the Cybertruck.

00:05:07.403 --> 00:05:12.503
by then that one roof panel has to carry fleet management data. It also has to

00:05:12.503 --> 00:05:17.263
carry navigation updates. It also has to carry passenger entertainment and it

00:05:17.263 --> 00:05:21.843
has to carry high-resolution video for remote oversight. That is four streams

00:05:21.843 --> 00:05:26.723
sharing the same antenna surface. They share the same power budget too. The design

00:05:26.723 --> 00:05:30.903
has to rank those jobs without creating a single point of failure. A patent

00:05:30.903 --> 00:05:35.203
already covers the physical mounting. That filing is what drops after market

00:05:35.203 --> 00:05:40.103
brackets. It also cuts service calls tied to weather exposure over the life of the car.

00:05:40.603 --> 00:05:45.623
From a cost standpoint, moving the antenna inside the body is what makes those mounts and those

00:05:45.623 --> 00:05:51.003
weather calls go away. Buyers are then locked into Tesla's ecosystem for the life of the vehicle.

00:05:51.523 --> 00:05:56.383
The hardware is not built for easy removal. It is not built for a third-party swap either.

00:05:57.003 --> 00:06:01.843
Connectivity revenue then rides on the car itself. It is no longer a separate subscription

00:06:01.843 --> 00:06:06.403
an owner could cancel. Spread that across a fleet of hundreds of thousands of vehicles,

00:06:06.903 --> 00:06:11.763
an optional accessory becomes a structural margin driver. Roof space that once held

00:06:11.763 --> 00:06:16.583
only a glass panel becomes a permanent data pipe. That changes the bill of materials.

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:20.843
It also changes the service relationship for as long as the car is on the road.

00:06:21.343 --> 00:06:26.203
Before we go, passenger features on that roof link are still waiting on a later software step.

00:06:26.203 --> 00:06:28.243
That's your Tesla news for today.

